# Conventional Commits

When creating a git commit in this repository, the subject MUST follow Conventional Commits:

```
type(optional-scope): summary
```

- English, imperative mood (`add`, not `added` or `adds`)
- Subject around 72 characters; no trailing period
- Body optional, separated by a blank line

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.

Examples: `feat: add task start endpoint`, `fix(users): return 404 when missing`, `ci: run e2e on pull requests`.

Do not pass `--no-verify` or `--no-gpg-sign`. The `commit-msg` hook must run.
